       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. A single dose of 1600 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for analgesia\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter that."
