      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for a dose that is twice the maximum daily limit. At 6,400 mg/day, the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm outweigh any benefit I can identify. I don't want to put it in the system where it could be given.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum standard dose\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n\nIf you need more analgesic or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen. One option is ibuprofen at the maximum dose plus scheduled acetaminophen.\n\nIf there's a clinical reason I don't know about, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, the order should go through pharmacy review and a direct order from you, not through me. Tell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
